{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1505739526,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDIxMTQ4OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842#issuecomment-330211489"},"message":"So one thing is how envars are converted into config items, and another thing is how config items are converted into Python dtypes. We should keep these things mentally separate.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505740262,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDIxNDgxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842#issuecomment-330214812"},"message":"I agree. Those are different layers. But they need to work together. If we allow config items to be empty, the conversions need to be able to deal with those items. And ATM they don't in general. And since config items can be set in different ways (not just env vars), we need to account for all of them.\nHowever, I'm not yet sure what is the right approach.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505824701,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDUyNTYwMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842#issuecomment-330525603"},"message":"Okay. As expected I'm running into this again ATM, since I'm enhancing possibilities to deal with known failures (ultimately in order to fix them, of course).\n\nRight now, I'm in favor of fixing this by just skipping empty env variables when loading them into `ConfigManager`. This means, that in case an env variable corresponding to a datalad config item was set to an empty string it actually gets the default value assigned as defined in `common_cfg.py`. Any objections to that approach?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505827073,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDUzNTg4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842#issuecomment-330535884"},"message":"I don't think I like that.  Being defined with an empty value is just that -- being defined with an empty value.  I do not think we should add magical sprinkles on top ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505827537,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDUzODA5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842#issuecomment-330538093"},"message":"Well, but what is this supposed to mean? If we have a datalad config item defined in `common_cfg.py` as sth, that is supposed to be a boolean for example and that has a default value - what's the desired difference between defining the corresponding env variable as `DATALAD_WHATEVER=` and not defining it at all?\nIs it reasonable to deal with it in the conversion to a bool? If so: Does empty equal `False`, while not defining it might evaluate to `True`, since this is the default? Does this make sense to you?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505827714,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDUzODk0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842#issuecomment-330538943"},"message":"Or do we just fail when it's empty, since this is an invalid value?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505834019,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDU3MjMyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842#issuecomment-330572326"},"message":"if expects bool,  and it is not among 0, 1, True, False, we could fail imho","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505895280,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMDc3OTE0NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1842#issuecomment-330779145"},"message":"Well, just failing might be okay. I feel it's somewhat counterintuitive to say \"I can't deal with an empty entry for that configuration, but if you don't have an entry at all I'm fine\", but I don't strongly oppose it.\nDo you agree to just fail,  @mih ?","files":null}]}